  "referenceNumber": "RUS3580",
  "remarks": "\nThe Secretary of State considers that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that SONGDOWON INTERNATIONAL CHILDREN’S CAMP is an “involved person” under the Russia (Sanctions) (EU Exit) Regulation 2019 because it is and has been responsible for and provides support for policies or actions which undermine or threaten the territorial integrity, sovereignty or independence of Ukraine, by engaging in and providing support for the Government of Russia’s programme for the forced deportation and re-education of Ukrainian children.\n",
